Z||000000||theogre||08-12-2001||09:41 PM||||I finally found my hard copy of the VIN sheet for each year.<P>The reason for confusion when decoding VIN numbers for 1984 GM product is that 1984 product doesn't use the same layout as 85 and up cars.<P>What this means is that all 1984 Fiero will read 1G2A in positions 1-4. <P>positions 1-3 are the same as later years.<P>Position 4 is always A.<BR>A is the restraint system code. "Non passive manual belts"<P>position 5<BR>E Coupe<BR>F SE<BR>M Sport Coupe<P>postition 6 & 7 is body type.<P>position 8 is engine code.<BR>Always R 4 cyl for 1984<P>postion 9 is the check digit.<BR>The method to calculate the check digit is in the Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standards.<P>position 10 is always E for 1984<P>the rest is the serial number.<P>------------------<BR><I><B>Screamin Yellow Zonkers... If it's Screamin and Yellow, I ain't eatin it.</B></I>||||reg||10
Z||000001||KRMFiero||08-12-2001||10:05 PM||||I always was wondering about that<P>thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
